{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1488290-stephen-strange","id":1488290,"title":"Stephen Strange?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-07-28T16:28:06-07:00","id":1488290,"title":"Stephen Strange?","content":"How would you build Stephen Strange as a newbie mage? Say, about the start of the third act in the first movie.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-28T17:00:23-07:00","id":1488292,"title":"","content":"As a member of the Akashic Brotherhood, probably.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-28T17:32:57-07:00","id":1488296,"title":"","content":"No, the exoticized Eastern aesthetics aside, his paradigm is all about dealing with and drawing on various extra dimensional alien powers. No group in Mage is a perfect fit for that, but Hermetics come closest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-28T18:08:31-07:00","id":1488297,"title":"","content":"The Eastern aesthetics have nothing to do with it. He's a man who was deeply entrenched in the modern world's web of ignorance and desire, consumed by his own vanity. The accident and accompanying loss of fine motor skills is the first step on the path out of suffering and eventually being able to see past the illusion of Reality. The Brotherhood also draw on various spiritual beings, from the Three Ministers of the Sam Chien down to the various spirits and ghosts of the Jnani. While he's probably a natural at Jivahasta, he needs to work on Prajna, Sunyakaya, and especially Tricanmarga.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-28T19:09:04-07:00","id":1488305,"title":"","content":"Frankly, I'd give him a few Wonders and be done with it. What magic did <i>he</i> perform, as opposed to having his cape fly him around, having his sling ring open portals, or having the Time Stone rewind time? <br /> <br /> Okay; there was that whole training montage where he was studying books of mysticism in astral form while his body slept. That would be some Mind magic. He definitely <i>doesn't</i> have Life magic, or else he would have used it to heal his crippled hands. Beyond that, I don't know. <br /> <br /> If I had to squeeze him into a Tradition, I'd pick the Order of Hermes. The Order isn't strictly European, you know; I believe that one of the newer Houses actually consists of former Wu Lung mages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-29T02:06:33-07:00","id":1488340,"title":"","content":"No one of Consequence makes a strong basic argument. And Dataweaver is undermined by the fact that the Wu Lung are Confucians, and would sneer at Buddhist thought. <br /> <br /> I'll go with the fact that in the original stories Dr. Strange goes to Tibet. In the early and mid Twentieth century Tibet was synonymous with mystic insight and ancient wisdom. When Mage first came out the nine traditions reflected stereotypes of magic users in American popular culture. <br /> <br /> On that basis No One of Consequence wins hands down. The AK Brothers got all the Tibetan stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-29T02:21:32-07:00","id":1488343,"title":"","content":"I'd probably make a Hermetic with Forces 3 and Spirit 3; then add any merits allowed to represent his intellect; and get flaws to represent his messed up hands and big ego. Then give him whatever wonder level is needed for a time reset wonder and/or a flying living cape thing. I'd definitely try to make sure he had Int 5, Medicine 5, Occult/Esoterica 5, and a decent level of physical fitness and melee combat capability. If I were using the older books, and can fit it in, I'd get that Merit where you are trained by 2 traditions. Hermetics and Akashics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12480,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","user":"Spacecat","date":". 07-29-2022, 05:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-29T03:16:11-07:00","id":1488348,"title":"","content":"As for Hermetics over Akashics, i would argue that the resource material used by the sorcerers is Hermetic and the Akashics aren't likely to worry too much about such written sources;<br /> The Book of the Invisible Sun is probably based on Splendor Solis; a rennaissance alchemical text<br /> Astronomia Nova is a western astronomy book<br /> Codex Imperium sounds like a latin text<br /> Key of Solomon is a real world Hermetic favorite<br /> Book of Cagliostro is likely the tome of Giuseppe Balsamo, aka Count Alessandro di Cagliostro; who in WoD would seem more Hermetic than anything else<br /> Maxim Gorky might be a fictional Theosophical work by Maxim Gorky... maybe.<br /> and real world Hermetic occultists have a long history of looking into eastern esoteric material, thus requiring knwledge in Classical Sanskrit<br /> The Akashayana would probably transmit most of their understanding through memorized forms, esoteric and mundane exercises, and meditative practices; and would likely have incorporated reincarnation into their protocol for what they do when their members die.<br /> <br /> That said, the mystic group that Dr. Strange is from is like an odd mix of Akashic and Hermetic and I'd go so far as to ask my storyteller if my character can be trained under a (probably now dead) master who studied under both traditions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-29T07:50:31-07:00","id":1488358,"title":"","content":"It probably isn\u2019t possible to match the movie Stephen Strange with anything in MtA. At best it might be some motifs and trends. Whatever group Strange learns from has both some aesthetic trappings of both eastern and western traditions. But most of the magic he uses is not possible in MtA without a potentially lethal paradox backlash. <br /> <br /> But a character inspired by Strange is fine for a starting point.<br /> <br /> I will use some of the mechanical suggestions here, and probably place the character in the Ex Misc. houses of the Order.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-29T08:06:47-07:00","id":1488359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1488290-stephen-strange?p=1488292#post1488292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a member of the Akashic Brotherhood, probably.</div> </div> </div> </div>Order of Hermes, beyond any doubt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-29T08:13:49-07:00","id":1488363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1488290-stephen-strange?p=1488358#post1488358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It probably isn\u2019t possible to match the movie Stephen Strange with anything in MtA. At best it might be some motifs and trends. Whatever group Strange learns from has both some aesthetic trappings of both eastern and western traditions. But most of the magic he uses is not possible in MtA without a potentially lethal paradox backlash. <br /> <br /> But a character inspired by Strange is fine for a starting point.<br /> <br /> I will use some of the mechanical suggestions here, and probably place the character in the Ex Misc. houses of the Order.</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely, House Ex Miscellania all the way. Those guys, despite some oriental aesthetics and some pseudo buddhism, they rely on knowledge spread by intellectual pursuit, memoraziation of formulae and specific &quot;spells&quot;, which is totally hermetic, rather than altered mental states, inner spiritual contemplation and body exercizes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-30T05:00:17-07:00","id":1488450,"title":"","content":"Why force him into anything? Make up your own tradition, take parts of the Akashic martial tradition and keeping of the record of time, take ritualistic practices and willigness to engage with anything in the cosmos of the OoH, and add a dose of the Pulp tradition/Theosophist Etherites. Call them The Followers of the Sorceror Supreme, Children of Vishanti Or Guardians of Agammoto.<br /> <br /> Done, you have a whole new faction with history and tradition, possibly alliances and conflicts with Akashics and Wu Lung and a style of their own.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-30T19:08:37-07:00","id":1488521,"title":"","content":"This is the first time this player has been in MtA game the first time they have crated a MtA character. They need some guidance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-30T21:22:49-07:00","id":1488530,"title":"","content":"Should all be fine as long as both you and the storyteller communicate your ideas to each other and come to agreement. I guess don't worry too much about tradition when doing character creation and just make Dr. Strange as you see him, then you and your Storyteller can try and fit him into the setting together. If you're stuck on details, just put a placeholder and then once everything's on there you can change what doesn't seem to fit; folllowing your instincts and the advice of your Storyteller.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-31T01:45:52-07:00","id":1488541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1488290-stephen-strange?p=1488521#post1488521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is the first time this player has been in MtA game the first time they have crated a MtA character. They need some guidance.</div> </div> </div> </div>What better way than to have the ST give him a support structure they can recognize and identify? It's a ready NPC faction for any kind of a chronicle.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-31T02:36:35-07:00","id":1488545,"title":"","content":"The problem with proposing a new faction is it puts a bit more work on what might be a new Storyteller to the setting.<br /> That said, it's a fair proposal and could come out really great if the Storyteller is aligned with it... Not so much if it doesn't align with their vision and gaming style.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-06T21:49:56-07:00","id":1489389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1488290-stephen-strange?p=1488305#post1488305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Frankly, I'd give him a few Wonders and be done with it. What magic did <i>he</i> perform, as opposed to having his cape fly him around, having his sling ring open portals, or having the Time Stone rewind time?<br /> <br /> Okay; there was that whole training montage where he was studying books of mysticism in astral form while his body slept. That would be some Mind magic. He definitely <i>doesn't</i> have Life magic, or else he would have used it to heal his crippled hands. Beyond that, I don't know.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was half done writing a long list of everything he did in Infinity War, Multiverse of Madness, etc but I just realized you meant by the third act of the 1st movie. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","name":"Alucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2078_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"811"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-07T00:14:58-07:00","id":1489397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1488290-stephen-strange?p=1488521#post1488521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is the first time this player has been in MtA game the first time they have crated a MtA character. They need some guidance.</div> </div> </div> </div>The most important thing is that both of you are on the same page. Mage the Ascension has Paradox while the Marvel movieverse does not. If the player is thinking that they'll be flying around tossing out lightning bolts and acting anything like Dr. Strange does in the movies, he could end up in finding the game stifling or annoying. For the most part I think the first Matrix movie is a good idea for the way a Mage game functions insofar as most of the action takes place away from the public eye (other than the helecopter scene there aren't too many witnesses and many of those end up dead) rather than in the middle of the city the way most Marvel movies do.<br /> <br /> I'm reminded of a game when my player group asked me to run a ninja campaign. Okay, sounded neat. I spent a lot of time writing up background, creating a huge cast of characters and modifying pieces of the Mage system. So I made this dark, gritty game that took place in the 1700's and involved the PCs being part of a ninja clan that was caught up in an existential battle against another ninja clan that had the ear of the Tokugawa Shogunate and had made an alliance with demons in order to wipe out of the PC's clan to settle past disputes that had happened hundreds of years earlier and both clans were stuck playing through the grudges of elders who were long dead.<br /> <br /> I was enjoying where things were going but the players weren't really engaged and I couldn't figure out why. After about the third session I was really stumped and one of the players finally said, &quot;Well yeah I know we asked for a ninja game and you did a lot of work, but we were thinking of something more like Naruto.&quot; So, yeah...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 08-07-2022, 09:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}